KG42.register("rules-10a633653cef0429d8f329fa",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R012","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R012","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","name":"Supply submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The supply component must report generation separately from demand in the submitted energy bid, rather than reporting only overall net demand. Scope: MMR supply-component reporting in the energy bid at each time step.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.supply under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.supply"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"MMR supply-component reporting in the energy bid at each time step.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R012-V001","symbol":"x_t^{dis*}","meaning":"discharging power variable of the EV at time step t (denoted x_t^{dis*} in the generation component of the MMR energy bid)","kind":"operational","domain":"power quantity per time step t ∈ T (domain not specified in the cited A24 snippet)","unit":null,"indices":["t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R012-P001","symbol":"η^{dis}","meaning":"discharging efficiency parameter multiplying x_t^{dis*} in the generation component of the MMR energy bid","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R012-P002","symbol":"P_{PV,t}","meaning":"PV power output at time step t, subtracted from the discharging output in the generation component of the MMR energy bid","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The supply component must report generation separately from demand in the submitted energy bid, rather than reporting only overall net demand. Scope: MMR supply-component reporting in the energy bid at each time step.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"In the MMR mechanism, the generation (supply) component of the energy bid at time step t is defined as the EV discharging power times the discharging efficiency minus the PV power output: e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} η^{dis}) - P_{PV,t} for all t ∈ T.","expression":"e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis}) - P_{PV,t}, \\quad \\forall t \\in T","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R012-V001"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R012-P001","v141-c-R012-P002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-06"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-06","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r4__v141-a-M02-bidding","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.2","anchor_text":"(A24) the internal price in diﬀerent ways according to the relationship between total n is equal to ","equation_id":"A24","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The MMR mechanism requires each prosumer to provide the energy bid that contains both generation and demand at each time step separately rather than an overall net demand as that in the SDR mechanism:\n\ne^{bid} = e_{gen}^{bid} \\cup e_{dem}^{bid}\n= \\{ e_{gen,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis}) - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\}\n\\cup \\{ e_{dem,t}^{bid} \\mid e_{dem,t}^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + P_t^{must-run} \\right), t \\in T \\}  (A24)"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-bidding"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-06","quote":"The MMR mechanism requires each prosumer to provide the energy bid that contains both generation and demand at each time step separately rather than an overall net demand as that in the SDR mechanism:"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"5e611d3359e0e2ff0b8639ff743de0a69b048119cec5535bd056c77998813f72","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The MMR supply-submission rule has a source-supported mathematical definition for the generation (supply) component of the energy bid: e_{gen,t}^{bid} = (x_t^{dis*} η^{dis}) - P_{PV,t} for t ∈ T (A24). This is formalized as a supporting mathematical constraint over the frozen node bidding.supply. The rule's core procedural statement about reporting generation separately from demand remains not_formalized because the separate-reporting/union structure involves the demand component, which is outside this rule's single-node scope and is covered under the demand-submission rule. The union e^{bid} = e_gen^{bid} ∪ e_dem^{bid} is therefore not introduced here. Symbols x_t^{dis*}, η^{dis}, and P_{PV,t} are declared with source evidence. No nodes or edges are changed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C001","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Procedural requirement that the supply component reports generation separately from demand; it governs the bidding.supply node."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C002","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The equation defines the generation component of the energy bid owned by bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-V001","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The EV discharging power variable x_t^{dis*} feeds into the generation component of the MMR energy bid, which is the subject of bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-P001","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The discharging efficiency parameter η^{dis} scales the discharging power in the generation-bid component of bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-P002","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The PV power output P_{PV,t} is subtracted from the discharging output in the generation-bid component of bidding.supply."}],"revision_requests":["For full verification, re-extract the symbol definitions of x_t^{dis*}, η^{dis}, and P_{PV,t} from Appendix A.1; the supplied A24 evidence contains the generation-bid formula but not the symbol-definition sentences, units, or sign conventions."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
